  county: Sonoma
  trust_name: BRUCE A. RIFKIN Revocable Trust
  trust_date: May 9, 2024

@center 
  @h1
    LAST WILL AND TESTAMENT

    OF

    {{testator}}

I, {{testator}}, of State of {{state}} County of {{county}}, state of residence at the time of death, revoke any prior wills and codicils and make this my will.

@box
  MY **FAMILY**
@;


I have two children. Their names and dates of birth are: Danielle K. Jensen, born on September 6, 2007; and Lauren A. Groshone, born on March 8, 2011. My Personal Representative may accept these dates as conclusive in making any determination for which they are pertinent. All references to "my children" shall include my children as of the date of this instrument.
@1 
  My personal representative shall make payments from my estate as follows:
  My personal representative shall pay from the residue of my estate or
  shall direct the trustee of the {{trust_name}}, dated {{trust_date}},
  to pay, or both, as determined in the sole discretion of my personal representative.

@center
  ## ARTICLE ONE
  PAYMENT OF EXPENSES AND TAXES

@1 
  My personal representative shall make payments from my estate as follows:
  My personal representative shall pay from the residue of my estate or shall direct the trustee of the {{trust_name}}, dated {{trust_date}}, to pay, or both, as determined in the sole discretion of my personal representative.

@@1.1 the expenses of my last illness and funeral, my valid debts, the expenses of administering my estate, including non-probate assets;

@@1.2 any estate taxes except to the extent paid from other sources, provided that the estate taxes paid by my personal representative shall be apportioned in accordance with the directions set forth in the General Governing Provisions below.

@@1.3 All payments under the preceding provisions of this Article shall be made prior to the final allocation of assets under Article 3 of this instrument.

@center
  ## ARTICLE TWO
  SPECIFIC GIFTS

@2 If I have made one or more written lists, signed by me and otherwise prepared in accordance with the provisions of state of residence at the time of death Statutes, Section 524.2-513 then I give the tangible personal property described in such list or lists to the persons named in such lists who survive me. To be given effect, a list must be signed by me or in my handwriting and it must describe an item or items of tangible personal property and the intended recipient with reasonable certainty. In the case of any inconsistent dispositions, the most recent disposition shall control. If no such list is found within thirty (30) days after my death, any dispositions made by such a list shall abate to the extent that the Personal Representative has distributed or disposed of such property.

@center
  ## ARTICLE THREE
  RESIDUARY ESTATE

@3 I give my residuary estate as follows:

@@a All to the trustee of the {{trust_name}}, dated {{trust_date}}, to be added to the trust estate and disposed of according to the terms thereof in effect at my death.

@@b If the trust fails for any reason, the residuary estate shall be distributed equally to my children who survive me, per stirpes.

@center
  ## ARTICLE FOUR
  FIDUCIARY PROVISIONS

@4 Appointment of Personal Representative.

@@a I appoint my daughter, Danielle K. Jensen, as my Personal Representative.

@@b If Danielle K. Jensen is unable or unwilling to serve, I appoint my daughter, Lauren A. Groshone, as successor Personal Representative.

@@c My Personal Representative shall serve without bond.

@5 Powers of Personal Representative.

@@a My Personal Representative shall have all powers conferred by law and the following additional powers, to be exercised in a fiduciary capacity:

@@@i To sell, lease, or exchange any property of my estate;
@@@ii To borrow money and encumber estate assets;
@@@iii To continue any business interest;
@@@iv To compromise claims;
@@@v To distribute in cash or in kind.

@center
  ## ARTICLE FIVE
  GENERAL PROVISIONS

@6 Definitions.

@@a "Survive" or "surviving" means living for at least thirty (30) days after my death.

@@b "Descendant" means a child, grandchild, or more remote descendant.

@7 Governing Law.

This will shall be governed by the laws of the State of {{state}}.

@pagebreak

